Check for new JusPrin versions on JusPrin's own GitHub releases

OrcaSlicer's update check is replaced by JusPrin's: app_update_check
hands it over, so OrcaSlicer's request never goes out and its "new
version" window no longer opens at startup. JusPrin asks its own GitHub
releases once a day (Updates/UpdateCheck, ReleaseFeed, UpdateRecord) and
compares against its own version, 2.0.0 (Updates/Version.hpp).

Preferences > Updates shows the result: up to date, checking, couldn't
check, or a new version with its release notes, "Download" (opens the
release page; nothing is installed in the app yet) and "Skip this
version". The "New JusPrin versions" checkbox switches the daily check
off and carries the privacy note. A Microsoft Store install says its
updates come from the Store. Help > Check for Updates runs the check and
opens Updates.

